From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:05:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Implement Credential Management's request and create
 algorithms

navigator.credentials.get() and create() rejected as not implemented.
They now run the spec's "request a credential" and "create a credential"
algorithms: the relevant credential interface objects, the types allowed
in one get() request, origin-bound types and opaque origins, the
environment's active credential types, whether the caller is same-origin
with its ancestors, each type's permissions policy feature, and abort
signals. A small registry describes each credential type the way the
spec's credential type registry does.

PasswordCredential and FederatedCredential now come from create() as
from their constructors. Ladybird has no credential store, so get()
finds no stored credentials and resolves with null, store() checks its
arguments without persisting anything, and preventSilentAccess() has no
flag to set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
